// Bitcoin Script Example: Conditional Execution
//
// Transaction version: 2
// It keeps every intermediate value on the stack to show the steps, and
// version 1 requires exactly one item at the end.
//
// Demonstrates IF/ELSE/ENDIF control flow

// Example 1: Simple IF statement
100
dup 50 greaterThan

if
  1000 add
else
  1000 sub
endIf

// Stack: [1100] because 100 > 50

// Example 2: Nested conditionals
50
dup 0 greaterThan

if
  dup 100 lessThan
  if
    // Number is between 0 and 100
    1 add
  else
    // Number is >= 100
    1 sub
  endIf
else
  // Number is <= 0
  negate
endIf

// Stack: [1100, 51] because 50 is between 0 and 100

// Example 3: Using notIf
0
notIf
  // This executes because stack top was 0 (false)
  999
endIf

// Stack: [1100, 51, 999]
